WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.858 --> 00:00:04.225
Hall B gets its power from a cable and a transformer.

2
00:00:05.258 --> 00:00:08.683
A transformer changes one AC voltage into another.

3
00:00:09.724 --> 00:00:11.477
Four topics follow that path.

4
00:00:12.207 --> 00:00:14.726
First the transformer and how it ages.

5
00:00:15.788 --> 00:00:19.306
Then the cables and how a connection is built and supplied.

6
00:00:20.652 --> 00:00:23.659
The first topic is The transformer and its station.

7
00:00:24.372 --> 00:00:29.004
In hall B it changes medium voltage into low voltage for the machines.

8
00:00:30.045 --> 00:00:32.448
It has two windings round an iron core.

9
00:00:33.162 --> 00:00:36.610
The turns ratio sets how far the voltage goes down.

10
00:00:37.612 --> 00:00:41.188
With the tap changer you adjust that ratio in small steps,

11
00:00:41.385 --> 00:00:43.045
usually with the power off.

12
00:00:44.329 --> 00:00:47.464
The second topic is Loading, ageing and condition.

13
00:00:48.180 --> 00:00:51.164
Heat slowly breaks down the paper in the windings.

14
00:00:51.878 --> 00:00:53.852
That is why it has cooling ribs.

15
00:00:54.901 --> 00:00:56.701
A short peak does little harm.

16
00:00:57.460 --> 00:01:01.512
Weeks too high cost a lot of life, so you look at the whole load profile.

17
00:01:02.509 --> 00:01:06.131
For a large transformer the oil says a lot about its health.

18
00:01:06.844 --> 00:01:08.620
You test it with a DGA.

19
00:01:09.896 --> 00:01:12.717
The third topic is Cables and cable faults.

20
00:01:13.425 --> 00:01:16.316
In the Netherlands almost all medium voltage and

21
00:01:16.351 --> 00:01:19.114
low voltage runs through underground cables.

22
00:01:20.130 --> 00:01:22.173
Cable lengths are linked with joints.

23
00:01:22.908 --> 00:01:25.358
They are made by hand and form the weak spot.

24
00:01:26.425 --> 00:01:30.837
If a cable fails, you first pre-locate the spot with a reflectometer.

25
00:01:31.631 --> 00:01:33.500
That tells you roughly where to dig.

26
00:01:34.808 --> 00:01:38.199
The fourth topic is Connections, standards and supply.

27
00:01:38.913 --> 00:01:43.163
A new connection goes through five steps, from request to execution.

28
00:01:44.283 --> 00:01:47.754
The work itself often takes only one or two days.

29
00:01:48.457 --> 00:01:52.335
The rest is waiting, for example for a permit or a transformer.

30
00:01:53.344 --> 00:01:58.058
To deliver faster, operators choose standards and sign a framework agreement.

31
00:01:59.175 --> 00:02:01.543
Then the installer connects the cables.

32
00:02:02.243 --> 00:02:04.170
The power goes to the switchboard.

33
00:02:05.509 --> 00:02:06.275
The whole map.

34
00:02:07.011 --> 00:02:11.550
Transformers and cables is the third station of Energy and the grid.

35
00:02:12.584 --> 00:02:14.314
Every topic has four levels.

36
00:02:15.345 --> 00:02:18.375
Start with How a transformer works at Basics level.

37
00:02:19.115 --> 00:02:21.820
That lesson shows how the voltage goes down.

38
00:02:22.887 --> 00:02:27.484
At Working knowledge level it is about the substation, how far you may load,

39
00:02:27.670 --> 00:02:29.830
cable faults and standardisation.

40
00:02:30.832 --> 00:02:34.256
At Advanced level it is about losses, reading the oil,

41
00:02:34.419 --> 00:02:36.938
testing cables and buying transformers.

42
00:02:37.966 --> 00:02:41.519
At Expert level it is about the voltage, the fleet view,

43
00:02:41.670 --> 00:02:45.141
how much current a cable can carry and the replacement wave.

44
00:02:46.151 --> 00:02:50.331
Every lesson and every film in this module has a place on this map.
